Crisp-seared chicken baked in a tropical sweet Hawaiian sauce with vibrant red bell pepper and pineapple tidbits.

*Adapted from [The Recipe Critic](https://therecipecritic.com/2015/07/baked-sweet-hawaiian-chicken/).*

## Ingredients

### Chicken
- 3–4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts, cut into bite-sized pieces
- Salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 1 ½ cups cornstarch
- 3 large eggs, beaten
- ¼ cup canola oil (for searing)

### Sweet Hawaiian Sauce
- 1 cup pineapple juice
- ½ cup brown sugar
- ⅓ cup soy sauce
- 1 teaspoon minced garlic
- ½ tablespoon cornstarch
- 1 red bell pepper, chopped
- 1 can (20 oz) pineapple tidbits, drained

## Instructions

1. **Prep the Oven and Chicken:** Preheat your oven to 325°F (165°C). Lightly grease a 9x13-inch baking dish. Cut chicken breasts into bite-sized pieces and season with salt and black pepper.
2. **Dredge in Cornstarch then Egg:** Place cornstarch in one shallow bowl and beaten eggs in another. Dredge each piece of chicken in cornstarch first (shaking off excess), then dip into the egg to coat completely.
3. **Brown the Chicken:** Heat ¼ cup canola oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken in batches for 2 to 3 minutes until golden brown on all sides (they will finish cooking in the oven). Transfer the browned chicken into the baking dish.
4. **Whisk the Sauce:** In a medium bowl, whisk together the pineapple juice, brown sugar, soy sauce, minced garlic, and ½ tablespoon cornstarch until smooth. Fold in the chopped red bell pepper and drained pineapple tidbits.
5. **Bake and Stir:** Pour the sauce and fruit mixture evenly over the chicken. Bake uncovered at 325°F for 1 hour. Stir the chicken every 15 minutes so the sauce caramelizes and glazes each piece evenly.
6. **Serve:** Let stand for 5 minutes off heat so the sauce thickens into a glossy glaze. Serve hot over steamed jasmine or white rice.

## Notes

- **Stirring is Key:** Stirring every 15 minutes allows the cornstarch-egg crust on the chicken to soak up the sauce and form a sticky glaze without burning.
- **Bell Pepper Variations:** Add green or yellow bell peppers for additional color and crunch.
